# Fetchlinks publisher environment -- copy to runtime/publisher.env, mode 0600.
#
# Read only by fetchlinks-publish.service and fetchlinks-retain.service. The
# collector unit deliberately has no EnvironmentFile at all, so this credential
# never enters the process that fetches from several hundred untrusted sites.
#
# Use the fetchlinks_publisher role, not the database owner: it can write
# content and read the catalog, and can do no DDL.
#
# Use the DIRECT endpoint, not the pooled one. psycopg3 promotes a statement to
# a server-side prepared statement after a few executions, and Neon's pooled
# endpoint is PgBouncer in transaction mode, where prepared statements do not
# survive. Pooling exists for Vercel, which opens many short-lived connections;
# this is one hourly process opening one connection, so it gains nothing from a
# pooler and would have to disable prepared statements to use one safely.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile is not a shell: do not quote the value, do not export.

FETCHLINKS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fetchlinks_publisher:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
